2026-11-07T05:17:01.2312292Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-07T05:17:01.2323588Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-07T05:17:01.2324283Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-07T05:17:01.2325072Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-07T05:17:01.2325503Z 
2026-11-07T05:17:01.2325787Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-07T05:17:01.2326282Z 
2026-11-07T05:17:01.2326658Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-07T05:17:01.2327527Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-07T05:17:01.2327953Z 
2026-11-07T05:17:01.2328133Z If you would like to
2026-11-07T05:17:01.2328588Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-07T05:17:01.2328923Z 
2026-11-07T05:17:01.2329211Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-07T05:17:01.2329721Z   $ sh ./install-nix
2026-11-07T05:17:01.2329913Z 
